{"acceptance_length": 2.7731958762886597, "acceptance_lengths": [6, 5, 3, 3, 1, 1, 1, 4, 10, 6, 4, 1, 2, 1, 2, 2, 4, 6, 1, 3, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 5, 6, 4, 1, 5, 3, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 2, 2, 6, 2, 5, 1, 1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 4, 2, 6, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 1, 2, 5, 2, 4, 2, 5, 4, 1, 9, 1, 2, 2, 3, 1, 6, 5, 4, 4, 1, 3, 5, 2, 4, 1, 5, 1, 2, 6, 3, 2, 1, 3, 1, 1], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 34409766400, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 34409763328, "benchmark": "math500", "completion": "To find the length of the hallway, we need to first determine the speed of the robot. \n\nGiven that the robot takes 2.5 hours to travel 1 kilometer, we can calculate its speed as follows:\n\nSpeed = Distance / Time\nSpeed = 1 km / 2.5 hours\nSpeed = 0.4 km/h\n\nSince we want to find the length of the hallway in meters, we need to convert the speed from kilometers per hour to meters per second. \n\n1 kilometer = 1000 meters\n1 hour = 3600 seconds\n\nSpeed = 0.4 km/h = 0.4 * (1000 m / 1 km) / (3600 s / 1 h)\nSpeed = 0.4 * 1000 / 3600 m/s\nSpeed = 0.1111 m/s\n\nNow that we have the speed of the robot, we can use it to find the length of the hallway. \n\nGiven that it takes the robot 90 seconds to travel the length of the hallway, we can calculate the length as follows:\n\nLength = Speed * Time\nLength = 0.1111 m/s * 90 s\nLength = 10 m\n\nTherefore, the length of the hallway is 10 meters.\n\n\\boxed{10}", "decode_seconds": 5.84680079203099, "draft_calls": 97, "input_tokens": 103, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "7ad23f549833b34cbe25e588ccd8cb6980306e33defce755cddb56206030da50", "method": "relay_p_cross_family", "output_hash": "aa0c7d7a8e3f2bf982fdd8b15a7a32a5559bc0ad1fde959e9256c81ffd994ec2", "output_token_ids": [1271, 1505, 279, 3160, 315, 279, 51902, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1176, 8417, 279, 4732, 315, 279, 12585, 13, 4815, 22818, 430, 279, 12585, 5097, 220, 17, 13, 20, 4207, 311, 5944, 220, 16, 15395, 21037, 11, 584, 649, 11294, 1202, 4732, 439, 11263, 1473, 11303, 284, 32235, 611, 4212, 198, 11